  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(114.02pt, 357.65pt, "Plate structures are widely used in large-scale engineering fields such as ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 375.65pt, "aerospace, hull manufacturing, and construction. However, the plate structure is easily ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 393.67pt, "damaged during long-term service or when it is impacted by foreign objects. Such a ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 411.67pt, "damage may lead to serious safety accidents. Beamforming and L-shaped sensor ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 429.67pt, "cluster (LSSC) localization method can be used to locate the damage on the plate. ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 447.67pt, "However, when using beamforming or LSSC localization method to locate the ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 465.67pt, "damages on plate-like structures, there exists blind area. In this paper, by combining ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 483.67pt, "the beamforming and LSSC localization method, a fan-shaped sensor cluster is ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 501.67pt, "proposed through arranging five sensors in a fan shape, which can effectively reduce ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 519.67pt, "the blind areas. The positions of damages on the plate can be accurately detected by ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 537.67pt, "using two groups of fan-shaped sensor clusters and one sensor for transmitting the ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 555.7pt, "excitation signal. The feasibility of the fan-shaped sensor cluster localization method ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 573.7pt, "is verified through numerical simulations and experiments, and the results are ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 591.7pt, "compared with those obtained by using the T-shaped sensor cluster. The results show ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 609.7pt, "that the fan-shaped sensor cluster can more accurately identify the damages at ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 627.7pt, "different positions. Both simulation and experimental results indicate that the ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
