// arXiv source page 19
#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-19.png", width: 418.5pt), 88.5pt, 72pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.024pt, 85.94pt, "compared with the T-shaped sensor cluster, the fan-shaped sensor cluster achieves ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 105.38pt, "higher prediction accuracy when detecting damages close to the horizontal direction ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 124.94pt, "of the sensor array. For example, for the damages D2, D3, D5 and D8 which are close ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 144.38pt, "to the horizontal direction of the linear array, the error is large when the T-shaped ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 163.94pt, "sensor cluster is used for detection.")
  #line-at(278.69pt, 163.94pt, "However, the error is smaller when use the ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 183.38pt, "fan-shaped sensor cluster for localization. For damages in other directions, the ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 202.94pt, "fan-shaped sensor cluster can also detect them accurately  ")
  #line-at(114.02pt, 222.38pt, "The fan-shaped sensor cluster localization method enables more accurate damage ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 241.97pt, "localization. Moreover, among the aforementioned damage cases, the maximum ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 261.41pt, "prediction error does not exceed 8.64 mm. The experimental results thus confirm the ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 280.97pt, "feasibility of this method. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 15.96pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.024pt, 334.25pt, "5. Conclusion")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(114.02pt, 372.89pt, "In this paper, a fan-shaped sensor cluster structure is innovatively proposed")
  #line-at(496.18pt, 372.89pt, "to ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 392.47pt, "improve damage localization accuracy, taking into account the advantages of ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 411.91pt, "beamforming and LSSC location methods, by combining the advantages of ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 431.47pt, "beamforming and LSSC localization methods. Through arranging five sensors in a ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 450.91pt, "fan-shaped structure, the blind area of damage location can be effectively reduced by ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 470.47pt, "using this geometric structure. The damage location in the plate can be accurately ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 489.91pt, "detected by using a detection system composed of two groups of fan-shaped sensor ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 509.47pt, "clusters and an acoustic source for exciting signals. In order to verify the effectiveness ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 528.91pt, "of this method, an aluminum plate is used for simulation and experimental ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 548.47pt, "verification, and the prediction results are compared with those of the T-shaped sensor ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 567.94pt, "cluster. Both simulation and experimental results show that the proposed method can ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 587.5pt, "effectively improve the accuracy of damage location. ")
  #line-at(114.02pt, 606.94pt, "The fan-shaped sensor cluster proposed in this study enables more accurate ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 626.5pt, "localization of damage positions. Compared with the T-shaped sensor cluster, the ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 645.94pt, "fan-shaped sensor cluster can accurately locate the damage near the horizontal ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 665.5pt, "direction of the array. And the method is easy to operate, because there is no damage ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 684.94pt, "location blind area, the fan-shaped sensor clusters can be placed without any ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 704.5pt, "constraints on orientation or position. There is no need to solve complex nonlinear ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 723.96pt, "equations for data processing. The damage location method of plate structure based ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 743.52pt, "on fan-shaped sensor cluster provides a new theoretical method for damage location, ")
]

